WEBVTT

00:01:59.043 --> 00:02:02.214
This is from Thomas Edison,
from the beginning of the 20th century:

00:02:02.238 --> 00:02:05.874
"Sleep is a criminal waste of time
and a heritage from our cave days."

00:02:05.898 --> 00:02:07.081
Bang!

00:02:07.105 --> 00:02:09.146
(Laughter)

00:02:09.673 --> 00:02:14.765
And if we also jump into the 1980s,
some of you may remember

00:02:14.789 --> 00:02:17.139
that Margaret Thatcher
was reported to have said,

00:02:17.163 --> 00:02:18.604
"Sleep is for wimps."

00:02:18.628 --> 00:02:21.499
And of course the infamous --
what was his name? --

00:02:21.523 --> 00:02:23.961
the infamous Gordon Gekko
from "Wall Street" said,

00:02:23.985 --> 00:02:25.885
"Money never sleeps."

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:29.116
What do we do in the 20th
century about sleep?

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:32.481
Well, of course, we use
Thomas Edison's light bulb